  homeHowTitle: 'How it works',
  homeHowLede: 'Records enter the WAL first and are folded into pages after commit. No resident service is involved.',
  homeHowStep1Title: 'Open the file',
  homeHowStep1Body: 'Database.open parses the page layout and schema document, then replays any unfolded WAL.',
  homeHowStep2Title: 'Commit the write',
  homeHowStep2Body: 'A VOS write program lands inside a transaction boundary, records its commit sequence in the WAL, and rolls back as a whole on failure.',
  homeHowStep3Title: 'Fold the WAL',
  homeHowStep3Body: 'checkpoint() merges the WAL into the main file, after which a single .yydb file is enough to move the database.',
  homeCtaTitle: 'Start with one file',
  homeCtaBody: 'Install the Node package to open or create a database file. No service to deploy and no extra runtime.',

